1
00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:20,734
Powertron!

2
00:00:20,818 --> 00:00:23,320
Special Attack!

3
00:00:27,324 --> 00:00:32,162
Curses!
I'll get you next time, Powertron!

4
00:00:33,622 --> 00:00:34,998
Hold it, Kingburg!

5
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:37,209
Dammit! Did he get away?

6
00:00:37,292 --> 00:00:42,130
However, we Powertrons will uphold
the peace of the network!

7
00:00:42,214 --> 00:00:44,299
Yeah!

8
00:00:52,349 --> 00:00:53,827
That was nothing like the stuff on TV.

9
00:00:53,851 --> 00:00:55,811
That was so cheap!

10
00:00:58,397 --> 00:01:01,233
Man, that's like way too expensive.

11
00:01:01,316 --> 00:01:04,736
Like I said,
it's from that show in Hiroshima.

12
00:01:04,778 --> 00:01:06,154
The one I couldn't go to?

13
00:01:06,238 --> 00:01:10,534
When Rei went fumbling her song
'coz those guys started trouble...

14
00:01:10,576 --> 00:01:14,872
And this is the MiniDisc from when
Mima sang in Rei's place.

15
00:01:14,913 --> 00:01:17,040
It's a precious sample of
Mimarin's singing voice!

16
00:01:17,082 --> 00:01:19,835
Oh, yeah... Is that rumor true?

17
00:01:19,918 --> 00:01:21,295
Oh, that?

18
00:01:21,378 --> 00:01:24,047
Three left, only three left...

19
00:01:24,923 --> 00:01:29,052
Last issue of CHAMMINGBIRD...
only three left.

20
00:01:29,970 --> 00:01:32,014
400 yen... 400 yen...

21
00:01:32,097 --> 00:01:33,390
Yeah, I read about that too.

22
00:01:33,473 --> 00:01:36,310
I heard she's announcing it today
coz it's the last concert here.

23
00:01:36,393 --> 00:01:41,148
At a nothing show like this?
That's pretty cold of Mimarin!

24
00:01:41,231 --> 00:01:44,234
There's been lots of solo
activity going on lately...

25
00:01:44,318 --> 00:01:47,279
And only Mimarin's like
worthy of being an actress?

26
00:01:47,362 --> 00:01:49,406
Look, they're back.

27
00:01:49,448 --> 00:01:51,783
The guys that caused trouble last week.

28
00:01:51,867 --> 00:01:56,163
I just hope they don't make
a mess today, of all days.

29
00:01:58,290 --> 00:02:00,542
I'm getting nervous!

30
00:02:00,626 --> 00:02:02,419
Come on, sit still!

31
00:02:02,461 --> 00:02:04,963
Hey, what's up with this!?
This is all frayed!

32
00:02:05,047 --> 00:02:06,089
Don't look at me!

33
00:02:06,173 --> 00:02:08,967
- Get me some masking tape!
- Hello? Yes.

34
00:02:09,051 --> 00:02:11,637
Remember your entrance
in the second song, Mima!

35
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:13,430
Don't pressure me!

36
00:02:13,513 --> 00:02:14,598
I need a drink!

37
00:02:14,681 --> 00:02:17,481
- I'm sorry. I'll call you back.
- You can have drinks after the event.

38
00:02:17,559 --> 00:02:19,102
You're on!

39
00:02:22,814 --> 00:02:25,108
And it looks like they're set.

40
00:02:27,778 --> 00:02:32,449
Without further adieu, please welcome
to our stage... CHAM!!

41
00:03:04,314 --> 00:03:10,070
Got a question about your love?

42
00:03:10,153 --> 00:03:15,951
Send a cry for help and wait a bit.

43
00:03:16,034 --> 00:03:19,830
Love makes your heart race.

44
00:03:19,871 --> 00:03:23,041
If it means you're loved in the end...

45
00:03:23,125 --> 00:03:26,336
be much more aggressive...

46
00:03:26,378 --> 00:03:29,715
because you will get a chance.

47
00:03:29,798 --> 00:03:37,798
The angel of love smiles at you.

48
00:04:06,209 --> 00:04:10,881
Mima! Mima! Mima!

49
00:04:19,431 --> 00:04:22,476
Mima should be acting, not singing!

50
00:04:26,897 --> 00:04:28,732
I can't do this after all!

51
00:04:28,774 --> 00:04:30,525
Mika...

52
00:04:30,609 --> 00:04:33,361
They want her in a drama series.

53
00:04:33,445 --> 00:04:35,280
There are no better deals than this!

54
00:04:35,363 --> 00:04:38,116
She can act AND sing!
That should be all right!

55
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:41,453
Her schedule with the other two
is already starting to mismatch!

56
00:04:41,536 --> 00:04:45,290
She didn't go through those hard
lessons to become an actress!

57
00:04:45,373 --> 00:04:48,919
The TV producer praised Mima's acting!

58
00:04:48,960 --> 00:04:52,380
But what about MIMA'S feelings!?

59
00:04:53,465 --> 00:04:54,549
And wait a bit.

60
00:04:54,591 --> 00:04:58,386
Love makes your heart race.

61
00:04:58,470 --> 00:05:01,598
If it means you're loved in the end...

62
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:04,851
be much more aggressive...

63
00:05:04,935 --> 00:05:08,396
because you will get a chance.

64
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:16,279
The angel of love smiles at you.

65
00:05:28,708 --> 00:05:31,044
Thank you very much.

66
00:05:31,128 --> 00:05:35,173
It was a fun concert, but we
only have one song left...

67
00:05:35,257 --> 00:05:37,592
We just got here!

68
00:05:38,969 --> 00:05:45,600
Umm... Before our last song,
we have news to tell you...

69
00:05:46,309 --> 00:05:50,981
Um, I, Mima Kirigoe, had a fun
time as a member of CHAM...

70
00:05:51,022 --> 00:05:53,525
Out of the way!

71
00:05:53,567 --> 00:05:56,528
What did we do!? HUH!?

72
00:06:02,784 --> 00:06:04,995
Quit showin' off!
You're only a part-timer!

73
00:06:05,078 --> 00:06:06,246
Outta my face, ya asshole!

74
00:06:06,329 --> 00:06:07,664
YOU get out of here!

75
00:06:07,747 --> 00:06:10,792
What the hell!? Who are you
telling to leave, you fucker!?

76
00:06:10,876 --> 00:06:12,711
It wasn't me!

77
00:06:13,753 --> 00:06:16,590
What are you doing!? Get the hell
over here, whoever threw that!

78
00:06:16,673 --> 00:06:18,550
Go home! Go home!

79
00:06:18,633 --> 00:06:22,012
- Dammit!
- Go home! Go home! Go home! Go home!

80
00:06:22,554 --> 00:06:24,431
Them again!

81
00:06:24,514 --> 00:06:25,724
We're canceling the show!

82
00:06:25,807 --> 00:06:27,017
But today is!

83
00:06:29,186 --> 00:06:31,980
Shut up! Goddammit!

84
00:06:32,063 --> 00:06:35,984
Go home! Go home! Go home! Go home!

85
00:06:36,067 --> 00:06:37,569
Stop it!

86
00:06:44,117 --> 00:06:45,952
Today...

87
00:06:46,036 --> 00:06:49,039
Just today... I wanted to have
a good time with all of you!

88
00:06:50,540 --> 00:06:54,294
What attitude from some no-namer!

89
00:06:55,587 --> 00:06:57,297
You little!?

90
00:07:01,092 --> 00:07:03,386
What do you want, you freak?

91
00:07:03,428 --> 00:07:05,805
Let's go!

92
00:07:18,652 --> 00:07:25,533
A-Actually... as of today, I...

93
00:07:26,660 --> 00:07:29,412
As of today,
Mima will graduate from CHAM!

94
00:07:29,454 --> 00:07:32,916
- What!?
- Why?

95
00:07:35,502 --> 00:07:37,420
Thank you all.

96
00:07:37,504 --> 00:07:43,343
I'm really happy that I spent the last
2 1/2 years with you all as part of CHAM!

97
00:07:43,802 --> 00:07:50,350
I hope you'll support me as
I do my best as a rookie actress.

98
00:07:52,143 --> 00:07:55,981
So this will be my last song.
Please listen.

99
00:08:07,158 --> 00:08:09,661
Well, it totally makes sense from
the agency's point of view.

100
00:08:09,744 --> 00:08:12,080
Pop idols just don't make money... right?

101
00:08:12,163 --> 00:08:14,082
Metamorphosis, huh?

102
00:08:14,165 --> 00:08:18,253
I still remember well...

103
00:08:18,336 --> 00:08:22,465
that warmth you'd given me.

104
00:08:22,549 --> 00:08:29,389
It was in the gentle rays of sunlight.

105
00:08:31,099 --> 00:08:35,270
I had believed that...

106
00:08:35,353 --> 00:08:39,441
the days past when...

107
00:08:39,524 --> 00:08:47,490
we were in love, were everything.

108
00:08:47,574 --> 00:08:51,911
Now, embraced by the memories...

109
00:08:51,995 --> 00:08:56,041
I have become a coward.

110
00:08:56,124 --> 00:09:00,295
I am choosing to live a life that...

111
00:09:00,378 --> 00:09:02,047
I can't feel any...

112
00:09:02,547 --> 00:09:06,468
- Mimarin!
- Don't leave us! Don't quit!

113
00:09:12,724 --> 00:09:14,642
Mimarin! Mimarin!

114
00:09:14,726 --> 00:09:16,686
Thank you.

115
00:09:16,728 --> 00:09:20,148
I'm always looking at Mima's Room!

116
00:09:41,211 --> 00:09:45,298
Geez! This cheese already went bad!

117
00:09:58,812 --> 00:10:02,816
I'm sorry...
I forgot to feed you yesterday.

118
00:10:16,037 --> 00:10:18,957
The earthquake that happened
in Mie prefecture...

119
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:22,001
flattened towns throughout the region.

120
00:10:22,085 --> 00:10:28,007
The government reports 200 dead, but
the total number of victims are...

121
00:10:28,091 --> 00:10:34,055
yet to be determined since many
more are missing amid the rubble.

122
00:10:34,139 --> 00:10:37,183
Authorities have called in troops
for rescue operations...

123
00:10:37,267 --> 00:10:40,353
however, because the area
is already getting dark...

124
00:10:40,437 --> 00:10:43,356
Thanks for all the work over the years.

125
00:10:44,732 --> 00:10:47,902
Bye bye, Mima the pop idol.

126
00:10:55,493 --> 00:10:58,538
"Sing for us forever"...

127
00:10:58,705 --> 00:11:01,374
I really can't do that.

128
00:11:08,214 --> 00:11:14,804
"I always like looking into Mima's Room.
I've put up a link to Mima's Room."

129
00:11:14,846 --> 00:11:16,389
What is this?

130
00:11:30,695 --> 00:11:33,323
- Hello?
- Mima! You're home!

131
00:11:33,364 --> 00:11:34,908
Mom!

132
00:11:36,034 --> 00:11:39,204
Yeah, I'm fine! How are you?

133
00:11:40,455 --> 00:11:43,374
Really?

134
00:11:43,458 --> 00:11:47,462
Yeah. Today was the last one.
No more singing for me.

135
00:11:47,545 --> 00:11:50,465
I remember when you kept saying
you wanted to be a singer.

136
00:11:50,548 --> 00:11:53,593
This is my big chance!
I told you that already!

137
00:11:53,676 --> 00:11:57,055
Lately, we've all been looking
forward to each new single!

138
00:11:57,138 --> 00:12:01,643
Your uncle over in Yamaguchi
buys 20 copies every time!

139
00:12:01,726 --> 00:12:04,979
You just don't understand
this industry, Mom.

140
00:12:05,021 --> 00:12:07,607
Wasn't singing what you were best at?

141
00:12:07,690 --> 00:12:10,443
The pop idol image is suffocating me!

142
00:12:10,527 --> 00:12:13,238
Besides, nowadays pop idols are...

143
00:12:13,321 --> 00:12:17,367
Wait, I've got a call on the other line...

144
00:12:17,450 --> 00:12:19,911
Yes, Kirigoe here...

145
00:12:19,994 --> 00:12:20,994
Hello?

146
00:12:23,081 --> 00:12:25,291
Hello?

147
00:12:28,378 --> 00:12:32,423
Mom? Just a wrong number.

148
00:12:33,216 --> 00:12:35,468
Yeah, I know.

149
00:12:35,552 --> 00:12:37,845
Oh, wait! The bath!

150
00:12:38,388 --> 00:12:39,548
Call me back in five minutes.

151
00:12:46,104 --> 00:12:47,480
Oh, Mother!

152
00:12:50,024 --> 00:12:52,986
A fax? Who's it from?

153
00:12:58,533 --> 00:13:03,496
Traitor traitor traltor
TRAiTor TrAltoR TralTor

154
00:13:18,136 --> 00:13:20,513
Who are you?

155
00:13:21,347 --> 00:13:23,433
"Who are you?"

156
00:13:23,516 --> 00:13:25,893
"Who are you?"

157
00:13:41,826 --> 00:13:45,496
Do you know what that note means, Rumi?

158
00:13:51,336 --> 00:13:54,047
It's an Internet home page.

159
00:13:54,714 --> 00:13:57,091
Oh, that thing that's been popular lately!

160
00:13:57,175 --> 00:13:59,844
And what is it?

161
00:13:59,927 --> 00:14:02,096
How can I describe it?

162
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:04,599
It's kind of like computer networks.

163
00:14:04,641 --> 00:14:05,767
And?

164
00:14:05,850 --> 00:14:08,936
Considering that this person
"put up a link to Mima's Room"...

165
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:13,191
this "Mima's Room" thing
is the title of a web site.

166
00:14:13,274 --> 00:14:14,525
You don't get it, do you?

167
00:14:14,609 --> 00:14:15,985
Nope. Not one bit.

168
00:14:16,027 --> 00:14:17,320
All right!

169
00:14:17,403 --> 00:14:19,030
Sorry to keep you waiting.

170
00:14:19,113 --> 00:14:21,949
We're ready for the take!

171
00:14:27,622 --> 00:14:30,166
Don't make me laugh!

172
00:14:30,249 --> 00:14:32,710
You're laughing on your own!

173
00:14:32,752 --> 00:14:34,045
5 seconds!

174
00:14:34,128 --> 00:14:36,547
4, 3, 2...

175
00:14:39,008 --> 00:14:41,594
The younger sister of Rika,
the murder victim, is here.

176
00:14:41,678 --> 00:14:42,845
Would you like to see her?

177
00:14:42,929 --> 00:14:44,430
Mr. Yamashiro.

178
00:14:47,141 --> 00:14:52,271
Do you know why the culprit peels
off the skin of his victims?

179
00:14:52,355 --> 00:14:56,818
I assume he gets sexual stimulation
from such activities...

180
00:14:57,402 --> 00:15:00,738
- He wants to become one.
- Become... what?

181
00:15:00,822 --> 00:15:04,033
A woman... or...

182
00:15:04,951 --> 00:15:07,120
CUT!

183
00:15:07,954 --> 00:15:11,457
Eri Ochiai is a great actress after all!

184
00:15:11,541 --> 00:15:15,002
She's a completely different person
when the camera is rolling!

185
00:15:15,086 --> 00:15:16,337
That's good!

186
00:15:16,421 --> 00:15:19,132
NEXT! Scene 32!

187
00:15:20,133 --> 00:15:22,385
Rika's sister, you're on!

188
00:15:22,427 --> 00:15:24,137
Here!

189
00:15:25,179 --> 00:15:26,431
Hold this!

190
00:15:26,472 --> 00:15:27,098
Nervous?

191
00:15:27,181 --> 00:15:29,392
A bit.

192
00:15:33,771 --> 00:15:36,774
Not much to get nervous about
when you have only one line...

193
00:15:38,985 --> 00:15:41,571
How's our star actress?

194
00:15:41,612 --> 00:15:44,532
Mr. Tadokoro. She's just going on now.

195
00:15:48,411 --> 00:15:50,079
"Who are you?"

196
00:15:50,163 --> 00:15:51,748
"Who are you?"

197
00:15:51,831 --> 00:15:52,831
"Who..."

198
00:15:57,378 --> 00:16:00,506
That's what I mean!

199
00:16:23,821 --> 00:16:24,864
Good morning!

200
00:16:24,947 --> 00:16:26,282
Morning!

201
00:16:26,365 --> 00:16:27,617
Good morning.

202
00:16:28,701 --> 00:16:30,995
Hello, everyone.

203
00:16:31,078 --> 00:16:32,538
Good morning.

204
00:16:32,622 --> 00:16:34,332
Mr. Shibuya! You're here too?

205
00:16:34,415 --> 00:16:36,918
Hi, Eri. How's it going?

206
00:16:36,959 --> 00:16:41,547
Sir, your lines are too hard!
I don't want to do it anymore!

207
00:16:41,631 --> 00:16:43,800
Don't say that!

208
00:16:43,841 --> 00:16:48,429
But the story is really good!!
I love stuff like this!

209
00:16:48,471 --> 00:16:49,931
You're good at egging people on!

210
00:16:50,014 --> 00:16:54,811
Eri. There were this many fan
letters sent to the station!

211
00:16:54,894 --> 00:16:56,854
Thank you, Mr. Tejima.

212
00:16:56,896 --> 00:16:58,648
Kuro...

213
00:16:59,899 --> 00:17:01,651
Oh, this one's not for you.

214
00:17:02,610 --> 00:17:05,279
Well, keep up the good work.

215
00:17:05,321 --> 00:17:08,157
So, Sir, tell me!

216
00:17:08,199 --> 00:17:10,159
Who's the criminal?

217
00:17:10,243 --> 00:17:12,954
Sorry, can't tell you.
That'd spoil the fun.

218
00:17:15,289 --> 00:17:17,708
So what ARE you going to
do about the criminal?

219
00:17:17,792 --> 00:17:21,712
You're gonna have to
make your mind up soon.

220
00:17:23,130 --> 00:17:26,884
Good morning, Mr. Tejima! Mr. Shibuya!

221
00:17:26,968 --> 00:17:28,344
Oh, hello there...

222
00:17:29,470 --> 00:17:32,682
Mima's getting good reviews.
Even among station staff.

223
00:17:32,723 --> 00:17:37,311
If that's the case, don't you think
she's got too few lines?

224
00:17:37,979 --> 00:17:40,273
So he says, Shibuya.

225
00:17:40,356 --> 00:17:42,316
Hey, don't look at me!

226
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:47,321
Sir! Please! Make use of
Mima just a little bit more!

227
00:17:48,239 --> 00:17:51,200
But see... She's a pop idol, right?

228
00:17:51,242 --> 00:17:52,618
They're really hard to use...

229
00:17:52,702 --> 00:17:56,080
That's no problem!
She's done with being a pop idol!

230
00:17:56,163 --> 00:17:57,373
Really?

231
00:17:57,415 --> 00:18:00,918
We want to give her a
drastic image change, too.

232
00:18:01,002 --> 00:18:03,129
We're ready for the take!

233
00:18:04,505 --> 00:18:07,216
Oh, this is for Mima.

234
00:18:10,428 --> 00:18:12,221
"Who are you?"

235
00:18:12,305 --> 00:18:13,556
"Who are you?"

236
00:18:13,639 --> 00:18:15,266
5 seconds!

237
00:18:15,349 --> 00:18:18,394
4, 3, 2...

238
00:18:25,109 --> 00:18:26,319
Mr. Tadokoro!?

239
00:18:27,403 --> 00:18:29,322
Mr. Tadokoro!

240
00:18:30,489 --> 00:18:33,075
Mr. Tadokoro!!

241
00:18:37,288 --> 00:18:38,331
I'm all right...

242
00:18:39,248 --> 00:18:41,208
What the hell is this!?

243
00:18:41,250 --> 00:18:43,628
I think that letter just exploded!?

244
00:18:43,711 --> 00:18:45,630
Call an ambulance! An ambulance!

245
00:18:45,671 --> 00:18:47,298
Yes!

246
00:18:47,381 --> 00:18:51,344
Is a warning.
The next one will be REAL.

247
00:19:16,535 --> 00:19:18,955
We're all set now.

248
00:19:18,996 --> 00:19:21,374
Rumi, you're really amazing!

249
00:19:21,457 --> 00:19:25,252
I'll sign you up for online services now.

250
00:19:25,544 --> 00:19:27,296
Okay.

251
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:29,799
What do you think, Rumi?

252
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:31,008
About what?

253
00:19:31,092 --> 00:19:33,135
About that thing the other day.

254
00:19:34,095 --> 00:19:36,555
Oh, that...

255
00:19:36,639 --> 00:19:39,016
Credit card number...

256
00:19:39,058 --> 00:19:42,812
Shouldn't we have called the police?

257
00:19:42,853 --> 00:19:46,649
Mr. Tadokoro said not to.
We can't do anything about it.

258
00:19:47,775 --> 00:19:50,486
But it was a crime!

259
00:19:50,528 --> 00:19:53,656
And it might have been me!

260
00:19:54,281 --> 00:19:57,493
It's okay. It was just a prank.

261
00:19:57,576 --> 00:19:59,996
Fortunately,
Mr. Tadokoro wasn't badly hurt.

262
00:20:00,037 --> 00:20:03,374
So you shouldn't worry, Mima.

263
00:20:03,457 --> 00:20:06,669
Anyway, Mima, I'll explain all
of this so listen carefully.

264
00:20:06,711 --> 00:20:08,004
Okay!

265
00:20:08,045 --> 00:20:11,674
This is a browser for the World Wide Web.

266
00:20:11,757 --> 00:20:13,968
You launch it by double-clicking here.

267
00:20:14,010 --> 00:20:16,095
Wha? Double-clip?

268
00:20:16,178 --> 00:20:17,763
What are you going to do with a clip?

269
00:20:17,847 --> 00:20:19,181
But...

270
00:20:19,265 --> 00:20:23,310
See, next to "location" you enter the URL.

271
00:20:23,394 --> 00:20:25,229
It's not hard, is it?

272
00:20:25,312 --> 00:20:27,189
Come on, Rumi!

273
00:20:27,231 --> 00:20:30,026
Can't you explain it to me in Japanese?

274
00:20:30,067 --> 00:20:33,571
Boy! Why did you buy a computer when
you don't know anything about it?

275
00:20:33,654 --> 00:20:36,490
Because they said it was easy!

276
00:20:36,574 --> 00:20:39,493
Oh, all right. I'll explain it from
the beginning once more...

277
00:20:39,577 --> 00:20:41,537
Okay!

278
00:20:48,919 --> 00:20:52,548
H... T... T... P...

279
00:20:57,011 --> 00:20:58,554
Ooh, something came up!

280
00:20:59,597 --> 00:21:02,058
Hey, I'm doing pretty well!

281
00:21:02,099 --> 00:21:04,727
And now...

282
00:21:04,810 --> 00:21:06,520
There it is!

283
00:21:06,562 --> 00:21:08,564
Mima's Room

284
00:21:11,609 --> 00:21:12,901
Mima's Room

285
00:21:12,902 --> 00:21:13,902
Mima's Diary

286
00:21:13,903 --> 00:21:15,071
Mima's Diary What's this?

287
00:21:15,112 --> 00:21:16,489
"It was just terrible!"

288
00:21:16,572 --> 00:21:19,116
"I screwed up the choreography,
AND forgot my lyrics."

289
00:21:19,200 --> 00:21:21,786
"I feel so sorry to all my fans!"

290
00:21:21,869 --> 00:21:24,789
"This morning, when I got off
the train left foot first..."

291
00:21:24,872 --> 00:21:27,041
"was when all the bad stuff started."

292
00:21:27,124 --> 00:21:29,710
"I always make it a point
that my right foot..."

293
00:21:29,752 --> 00:21:31,921
"goes first into the
train and into the bath."

294
00:21:32,004 --> 00:21:35,216
Someone sure knows me! What's this?

295
00:21:35,299 --> 00:21:38,427
"Today was my 21st birthday."

296
00:21:38,511 --> 00:21:44,767
"Yukiko, Rei, and the staff at the agency
held a party for me. It was terrific!"

297
00:21:44,850 --> 00:21:48,562
"Coming home, I went grocery
shopping at the usual store."

298
00:21:48,604 --> 00:21:50,564
"I got mineral water and milk."

299
00:21:50,648 --> 00:21:53,359
"The milk just has to be Cow Brand milk."

300
00:21:53,442 --> 00:21:56,028
"I have to allow myself at
least this much luxury."

301
00:21:56,112 --> 00:22:00,282
"And food for my precious
fish, of course..."

302
00:22:00,366 --> 00:22:06,372
"May 12th. I was impressed with Eri
Ochiai's performance in Double Bind."

303
00:22:06,455 --> 00:22:09,250
"She's another person when
the camera is rolling..."

304
00:22:09,291 --> 00:22:10,543
What is all this?

305
00:22:10,626 --> 00:22:12,711
How do they know this much?

306
00:22:12,795 --> 00:22:15,297
Who are you?

307
00:22:15,381 --> 00:22:18,008
Who are you?

308
00:22:18,092 --> 00:22:20,886
Who are you?

309
00:22:20,970 --> 00:22:23,430
Who are you?

310
00:22:23,514 --> 00:22:28,853
Who are you?

311
00:22:30,896 --> 00:22:33,315
Who are you?

312
00:22:33,357 --> 00:22:36,902
I'm Dr. Toko Asamiya,
specializing in psychiatry.

313
00:22:36,986 --> 00:22:40,823
I was your late sister's psychiatrist.

314
00:22:40,906 --> 00:22:43,033
There are some things
I'd like to ask you.

315
00:22:43,117 --> 00:22:45,119
Detective Yamashiro! Another one!

316
00:22:45,161 --> 00:22:46,287
What!?

317
00:23:06,682 --> 00:23:09,768
This is the fifth victim...

318
00:23:12,688 --> 00:23:14,231
Just three shots.

319
00:23:16,525 --> 00:23:20,321
Is this work really worth leaving CHAM for?

320
00:23:20,362 --> 00:23:23,240
Rumi. Do you know how hard
it is to get a character...

321
00:23:23,282 --> 00:23:26,202
that reappears in a drama series?
Even a role like this?

322
00:23:26,243 --> 00:23:29,246
Yes, I do. But...

323
00:23:31,665 --> 00:23:36,879
This is where Mima proves if she can
be seen as a real actress or not.

324
00:23:36,962 --> 00:23:40,549
But we should sell Mima as a pop idol!

325
00:23:40,633 --> 00:23:45,512
Really. Times are different from when
Rumi Hidaka was a working pop idol.

326
00:23:45,554 --> 00:23:46,972
I know that.

327
00:23:47,056 --> 00:23:50,142
Nowadays, there are no places for
pop idols to appeal to the masses.

328
00:23:50,226 --> 00:23:53,646
This is the branch point that will
decide if Mima lasts or not.

329
00:23:53,729 --> 00:23:56,023
Well, excuse me for not surviving.

330
00:23:56,065 --> 00:23:57,816
Please, Rumi!

331
00:23:57,900 --> 00:24:02,529
There's nothing better than having Mima
be able to change into an actress!

332
00:24:02,613 --> 00:24:05,574
She came to Tokyo to sing...

333
00:24:05,616 --> 00:24:07,618
Think!

334
00:24:07,660 --> 00:24:11,580
On record sales we make
practically nothing!

335
00:24:13,958 --> 00:24:17,336
But I do wish that they'd
use her a little bit more...

336
00:24:17,419 --> 00:24:20,047
Sorry we're not that profitable!

337
00:24:20,589 --> 00:24:22,549
Good morning!

338
00:24:22,633 --> 00:24:25,719
How's the new CHAM going?

339
00:24:32,601 --> 00:24:35,938
Double Bind

340
00:24:46,282 --> 00:24:48,200
It's the pits!

341
00:24:48,284 --> 00:24:50,911
Double Bind... yeah, I saw it too.

342
00:24:50,953 --> 00:24:52,621
It was so boring!

343
00:24:52,705 --> 00:24:57,167
Why do all psycho-thrillers made
in Japan turn out that way?

344
00:24:57,251 --> 00:24:59,503
Mimarin's not in it!

345
00:24:59,586 --> 00:25:02,506
Oh yeah. How many scenes was
she in last week? Four?

346
00:25:02,589 --> 00:25:04,800
Three.

347
00:25:04,883 --> 00:25:08,262
Somebody save Mimarin! PLEASE!

348
00:25:09,305 --> 00:25:15,311
A HOME PAGE ON THE INTERNET:
You can make one too!

349
00:25:30,868 --> 00:25:33,149
This morning, when I got off
the train left foot first...

350
00:26:16,413 --> 00:26:18,082
Hey, It's Mimarin!

351
00:26:18,165 --> 00:26:18,874
Good morning!

352
00:26:18,957 --> 00:26:20,501
Good morning, Mimarin!

353
00:26:20,542 --> 00:26:21,811
Break a leg with that drama series!

354
00:26:21,835 --> 00:26:23,796
Hey, wait, Mimarin...

355
00:26:25,214 --> 00:26:29,510
Do they get all unfriendly when
they become actresses?

356
00:26:38,018 --> 00:26:40,437
Hit-And-Run at Shinkaido.

357
00:26:40,521 --> 00:26:43,982
Tadashi Doi (18), in critical condition.

358
00:26:56,578 --> 00:26:58,414
Good morning!

359
00:26:58,497 --> 00:26:59,706
Good morning, Mima.

360
00:26:59,790 --> 00:27:01,667
Cheers!

361
00:27:01,750 --> 00:27:04,002
Cheers!

362
00:27:06,338 --> 00:27:08,549
What's going on?

363
00:27:08,590 --> 00:27:10,634
CHAM's new single...

364
00:27:11,385 --> 00:27:15,139
Oh, wow! They got 83rd?

365
00:27:15,222 --> 00:27:18,100
We never even made the charts before.

366
00:27:18,183 --> 00:27:19,183
One, two...

367
00:27:22,646 --> 00:27:24,565
Congratulations!

368
00:27:25,858 --> 00:27:27,234
We did it!

369
00:27:27,317 --> 00:27:29,278
Now we've got to work together really hard!

370
00:27:29,361 --> 00:27:32,197
But will there be anyone in the audience?

371
00:27:32,281 --> 00:27:34,783
Sure there will be, Mima!

372
00:27:36,743 --> 00:27:40,080
Your next script.
It has a few more lines.

373
00:27:40,122 --> 00:27:41,457
Yeah.

374
00:27:41,999 --> 00:27:44,001
You've both done great!

375
00:27:44,084 --> 00:27:47,504
CHAM is totally okay being a duo!

376
00:28:04,480 --> 00:28:07,191
Hey, you. Are you currently
in any talent agency?

377
00:28:07,274 --> 00:28:09,359
I'm sorry, I'm in a hurry.

378
00:28:10,819 --> 00:28:12,154
Hey!

379
00:28:12,237 --> 00:28:14,948
Wouldn't you be interested
in being a model?

380
00:28:14,990 --> 00:28:17,242
Model?

381
00:28:17,910 --> 00:28:19,411
Cut!

382
00:28:25,834 --> 00:28:29,630
OK! We're going to move for the next scene!

383
00:28:32,549 --> 00:28:34,510
Who's that girl?

384
00:28:34,551 --> 00:28:37,095
I don't know.

385
00:28:38,680 --> 00:28:40,098
Hey, hey, hey!

386
00:28:40,182 --> 00:28:44,311
I saw next week's script, Shibuya.
You're wonderful!

387
00:28:44,394 --> 00:28:47,606
I didn't think it would come to this!

388
00:28:47,689 --> 00:28:50,108
To tell the truth,
I have an even more drastic idea.

389
00:28:50,192 --> 00:28:51,527
Fantastic!

390
00:28:51,610 --> 00:28:53,237
But...

391
00:28:53,320 --> 00:28:56,490
I wonder if it would be
all right for Mima...

392
00:28:56,532 --> 00:28:58,951
or rather, her agency.

393
00:29:07,084 --> 00:29:09,169
Mima's character,
Yoko Takakura, changes...

394
00:29:09,211 --> 00:29:13,173
personalities completely when she's
raped by the customers at a strip show.

395
00:29:13,257 --> 00:29:16,343
You're crazy! A rape scene!?

396
00:29:16,426 --> 00:29:19,239
She's the key figure in the second half
of the series! It's an important role!

397
00:29:19,263 --> 00:29:21,974
But Mima's a pop idol!

398
00:29:22,724 --> 00:29:24,393
Don't worry, Mima.

399
00:29:24,476 --> 00:29:27,396
We'll ask the producer and get it changed.

400
00:29:27,437 --> 00:29:29,565
Hey, hey. Wait a minute!

401
00:29:29,648 --> 00:29:33,110
The scripts are already behind schedule
as is, and the art staff is getting antsy!

402
00:29:33,151 --> 00:29:36,613
How will it look if we
make it worse by arguing?

403
00:29:36,697 --> 00:29:40,617
I even told Shibuya that she was
changing out from a pop idol!

404
00:29:40,701 --> 00:29:43,579
It's our job to protect the
celebrities in our agency!

405
00:29:43,620 --> 00:29:46,039
There's no way Mima can do such a thing!

406
00:29:46,081 --> 00:29:47,749
It's all right, Rumi.

407
00:29:48,417 --> 00:29:49,960
I'll do it.

408
00:29:50,043 --> 00:29:52,170
Because I decided that
I WILL become an actress.

409
00:29:52,254 --> 00:29:52,879
Mima!

410
00:29:52,963 --> 00:29:55,257
I see. You're really wonderful, Mima!

411
00:29:55,299 --> 00:30:00,262
This kind of thing is commonplace for
actresses! Jodie whatshername did it too!

412
00:30:00,304 --> 00:30:02,764
Mima, please think it out.

413
00:30:02,848 --> 00:30:04,826
Do you realize what will
happen as a result of this?

414
00:30:04,850 --> 00:30:08,437
It's not as if I'm really getting raped!

415
00:30:08,520 --> 00:30:11,898
Although... I'm sure my parents will
flip when they see me like that.

416
00:30:13,650 --> 00:30:17,571
Anyway, I'll do it.
I'll give it my best shot.

417
00:30:18,280 --> 00:30:20,574
Mima...

418
00:30:34,630 --> 00:30:36,465
I absolutely REFUSE to do it!

419
00:30:54,983 --> 00:30:58,612
Well, Mr. Director?
How does the set look?

420
00:30:58,695 --> 00:31:00,947
I'd prefer to shoot in a real club...

421
00:31:00,989 --> 00:31:04,660
but considering what we're filming,
nobody will let us shoot at their place.

422
00:31:04,701 --> 00:31:06,411
Sheesh!

423
00:31:06,995 --> 00:31:09,414
Please, I'm counting on you.

424
00:31:09,498 --> 00:31:13,251
Hey, hey, hey, come on, Yada!

425
00:31:13,335 --> 00:31:16,421
What are you going to do with just
the DATE of the next meeting!?

426
00:31:16,838 --> 00:31:20,050
That doesn't make for much of a meeting!

427
00:31:20,133 --> 00:31:21,426
OK here!

428
00:31:29,351 --> 00:31:31,895
We're ready to shoot!

429
00:31:32,688 --> 00:31:36,942
Scene 48, "The manager gets
dragged down", take 1!

430
00:31:37,401 --> 00:31:39,945
Ten seconds...

431
00:31:42,572 --> 00:31:46,201
5, 4, 3, 2...

432
00:32:08,265 --> 00:32:10,308
Mmmm! Looks good!

433
00:32:10,392 --> 00:32:13,270
Ex-pop idols sure make a nice scene!

434
00:32:14,312 --> 00:32:16,356
No! Stop! Let me go!

435
00:32:16,440 --> 00:32:18,316
Cut it off! Get off the stage!

436
00:32:18,400 --> 00:32:19,484
Shut the fuck up!

437
00:32:19,568 --> 00:32:21,045
Get out of here! I'll call the police!

438
00:32:21,069 --> 00:32:22,422
You think I give a shit about cops?

439
00:32:22,446 --> 00:32:23,155
Stop!

440
00:32:23,238 --> 00:32:24,489
Hands off!

441
00:32:24,573 --> 00:32:26,283
Stop it!

442
00:32:31,079 --> 00:32:33,331
Let me go! Stop it!

443
00:32:33,999 --> 00:32:36,543
Help! Help me! No!

444
00:32:45,594 --> 00:32:48,013
Please! NO!

445
00:32:48,388 --> 00:32:50,557
Cut!

446
00:32:53,518 --> 00:32:55,562
Hey, over there, hold your places!

447
00:32:59,858 --> 00:33:04,070
OK! Now move the cameras!

448
00:33:06,114 --> 00:33:07,949
I'm so sorry...

449
00:33:07,991 --> 00:33:09,576
Oh, no, it's all right.

450
00:33:10,368 --> 00:33:12,120
OK, next up, the rape scene!

451
00:33:12,204 --> 00:33:14,164
Everyone, get ready!

452
00:33:14,247 --> 00:33:16,917
Take 1! Rolling!

453
00:33:17,417 --> 00:33:22,422
No! Stop! No! No! Stop!

454
00:33:32,140 --> 00:33:35,477
Please! Stop!

455
00:33:35,519 --> 00:33:36,603
Cut!

456
00:33:37,729 --> 00:33:39,606
No, no, no! FASTER!

457
00:33:39,689 --> 00:33:41,650
Sorry!

458
00:33:41,733 --> 00:33:43,735
Once again, from the top!

459
00:33:43,819 --> 00:33:47,113
No break yet! Take 2!

460
00:33:53,370 --> 00:33:55,330
Please! Stop!

461
00:33:55,413 --> 00:33:57,749
No! Please! NO!

462
00:33:57,833 --> 00:34:00,126
Stop it! No!

463
00:34:14,182 --> 00:34:15,392
Please!

464
00:34:59,978 --> 00:35:03,231
Mimarin!!

465
00:35:26,421 --> 00:35:28,965
I'm so tired!

466
00:35:30,008 --> 00:35:32,636
Hey, where's Rumi?

467
00:35:32,802 --> 00:35:37,766
Hmm? Oh, she had a
meeting to go to for me...

468
00:35:37,849 --> 00:35:40,393
Hey, Mima...

469
00:35:40,477 --> 00:35:42,646
You know...

470
00:35:47,192 --> 00:35:49,110
Nothing. You tried so hard...

471
00:35:49,152 --> 00:35:51,172
As a reward for your efforts,
I'll treat you to a delicious meal.

472
00:35:51,196 --> 00:35:52,197
Lucky me!

473
00:36:14,052 --> 00:36:17,055
I'm home, fishies!

474
00:36:17,138 --> 00:36:19,724
I wonder if you're hungry yet?

475
00:37:08,398 --> 00:37:11,026
Of course I didn't want to do it!

476
00:37:11,109 --> 00:37:13,945
But I couldn't trouble all the people
who brought me this far!!

477
00:37:16,865 --> 00:37:18,992
See, didn't I tell you?

478
00:37:20,160 --> 00:37:22,537
Is that the job that what you wanted?

479
00:37:22,579 --> 00:37:25,331
That was the PITS!

480
00:37:40,430 --> 00:37:42,265
I don't want to do that drama anymore!

481
00:37:42,348 --> 00:37:46,394
The producer is a total pervert, and
my role is really screwed up!

482
00:37:46,478 --> 00:37:51,024
Singing in front of my fans has
GOT to be the best for me after all!

483
00:38:01,701 --> 00:38:04,120
Oh... that scene?

484
00:38:04,162 --> 00:38:07,832
Of course I would be lying if I said
I didn't have any hesitations...

485
00:38:07,916 --> 00:38:12,796
but I looked at it as a hurdle
I had to jump over as an actress.

486
00:38:13,713 --> 00:38:15,757
I heard the ratings went up.

487
00:38:16,800 --> 00:38:19,761
As always,
the public at large are all idiots.

488
00:38:20,011 --> 00:38:22,931
Yes. I'd like to be
recognized as an actress.

489
00:38:22,972 --> 00:38:24,599
Not as "the ex-pop idol"?

490
00:38:24,641 --> 00:38:25,725
You got it!

491
00:38:26,017 --> 00:38:29,270
I was fine coz Rei was
always the one I liked.

492
00:38:29,312 --> 00:38:32,273
I'm sure all the Mimarin fans
are crying right about now.

493
00:38:32,732 --> 00:38:38,613
But CHAM did teach me a lot. It was
a great experience in its own way.

494
00:38:38,696 --> 00:38:39,823
Yeah, totally!

495
00:38:39,906 --> 00:38:43,576
They're probably whining,
"That's not Mimarin!"

496
00:38:53,711 --> 00:38:58,675
Mima's Room

497
00:38:59,759 --> 00:39:02,720
What was YOUR day like?

498
00:39:04,139 --> 00:39:05,699
"Today, I was still a little depressed..."

499
00:39:05,723 --> 00:39:09,269
"but receiving e-mail from all of
you made me feel a little better."

500
00:39:09,310 --> 00:39:10,770
E-mail?

501
00:39:10,812 --> 00:39:14,149
"June 24: Help me, everyone..."

502
00:39:15,358 --> 00:39:20,572
"Everyone is forcing me to do it!
It's all the screenwriter's fault!"

503
00:39:20,655 --> 00:39:22,007
Help! Help! Help! Help! Help! Help!

504
00:39:22,031 --> 00:39:25,493
This... This isn't true!
I'm not writing any of this!

505
00:39:25,535 --> 00:39:29,247
Of course!
The REAL Mima is writing this!

506
00:39:31,875 --> 00:39:35,253
I know that deep down in your heart
you want to be a pop idol again.

507
00:39:35,336 --> 00:39:36,336
No!

508
00:39:36,379 --> 00:39:38,298
I'm no longer...

509
00:39:38,339 --> 00:39:40,383
No longer what?

510
00:39:40,466 --> 00:39:43,845
Oh, yeah, you're no longer a pop idol.

511
00:39:43,887 --> 00:39:46,931
You're a filthy woman now.

512
00:39:47,015 --> 00:39:50,643
Nobody likes idols with
tarnished reputations!

513
00:39:50,685 --> 00:39:52,562
That's not true! That's not true!

514
00:39:52,645 --> 00:39:55,315
Mimarin!

515
00:39:59,819 --> 00:40:03,823
You can't step back into
that spotlight now...

516
00:40:06,034 --> 00:40:08,661
But that's all right. I'M here.

517
00:40:10,622 --> 00:40:14,667
From now on, I'll be in the light,
and you'll be in the shadows.

518
00:40:16,711 --> 00:40:18,046
What are you saying!?

519
00:40:18,087 --> 00:40:20,173
Who in the world are you!?

520
00:40:20,632 --> 00:40:22,550
Nobody likes you anymore.

521
00:40:22,592 --> 00:40:24,886
You're tarnished! FILTHY!

522
00:40:24,969 --> 00:40:26,888
Stop! Stop it!

523
00:40:26,930 --> 00:40:29,807
I am not tarnished!

524
00:40:30,225 --> 00:40:31,434
Wait!

525
00:40:31,517 --> 00:40:33,519
WAIT!

526
00:41:16,813 --> 00:41:20,149
Love makes your heart race.

527
00:41:20,233 --> 00:41:23,403
If it means you're loved in the end...

528
00:41:23,444 --> 00:41:26,572
be much more aggressive...

529
00:41:26,656 --> 00:41:29,951
because you will get a chance.

530
00:41:30,034 --> 00:41:35,623
The angel of love smiles at you.

531
00:41:35,707 --> 00:41:38,209
Is anyone there?

532
00:41:47,010 --> 00:41:50,513
Can you see the angel's white wings?

533
00:41:50,596 --> 00:41:54,976
Or her eyes gazing at you...

534
00:41:55,059 --> 00:41:59,105
her sweet voice, her gentle hands?

535
00:41:59,188 --> 00:42:03,484
She is here just for you.

536
00:42:03,568 --> 00:42:07,864
She is protecting you...

537
00:42:07,947 --> 00:42:11,951
from somewhere nearby.

538
00:42:12,035 --> 00:42:16,622
Got a question about...

539
00:42:16,664 --> 00:42:20,335
Love makes your heart race.

540
00:42:20,418 --> 00:42:23,588
If it means you're loved in the end...

541
00:42:23,671 --> 00:42:26,632
be much more aggressive...

542
00:43:03,002 --> 00:43:05,671
It happened about
1 o'clock this morning.

543
00:43:06,464 --> 00:43:09,592
Hey, I called you last
night and you weren't in...

544
00:43:09,675 --> 00:43:13,638
"Oh shit! How did you know?"
Yeah, right.

545
00:43:13,721 --> 00:43:15,723
Did you see "Mima's Room"?

546
00:43:15,807 --> 00:43:18,393
Yeah, but is that really her?

547
00:43:18,476 --> 00:43:20,103
No clue.

548
00:43:20,186 --> 00:43:22,939
According to that page,
Mimarin's gonna be on stage today.

549
00:43:23,022 --> 00:43:24,482
No way!

550
00:43:25,024 --> 00:43:29,736
Police say Shibuya was stabbed umpteen
times with a sharp object...

551
00:43:29,737 --> 00:43:32,633
Popular Script Writer SLAUGHTERED!
The victim: Takao Shibuya (34)
Police say Shibuya was stabbed umpteen
times with a sharp object...

552
00:43:32,657 --> 00:43:37,203
It sure is a shocking incident, but
us worrying about it won't help.

553
00:43:37,245 --> 00:43:38,847
We have to put our minds on something else.

554
00:43:38,871 --> 00:43:41,707
But there was that letter bomb too...

555
00:43:42,708 --> 00:43:46,212
You think Mr. Shibuya's murder
is connected with that?

556
00:43:47,130 --> 00:43:50,007
I didn't say that...

557
00:43:50,091 --> 00:43:54,554
You watch too many TV tabloid shows.
Don't worry about it.

558
00:43:54,637 --> 00:43:58,724
You won't become a star
looking like that! Smile!

559
00:44:00,101 --> 00:44:03,229
Shibuya won the New Writers'
Prize in 1990, and then...

560
00:44:05,398 --> 00:44:06,482
Serves...

561
00:44:06,566 --> 00:44:07,358
you...

562
00:44:07,442 --> 00:44:09,735
right!?

563
00:44:19,328 --> 00:44:22,915
What's wrong? Mima! MIMA!

564
00:44:27,086 --> 00:44:30,089
But will Mima be all right?

565
00:44:30,131 --> 00:44:31,591
Why?

566
00:44:31,632 --> 00:44:35,011
That photographer specializes
in getting people to strip!

567
00:44:35,094 --> 00:44:36,762
So what?

568
00:44:36,804 --> 00:44:39,015
She's got that part down pat!

569
00:44:39,098 --> 00:44:41,851
I'm sure she's totally showing it
off in front of the photographer!

570
00:44:41,934 --> 00:44:43,394
Like, TOTALLY!

571
00:44:43,478 --> 00:44:45,938
Isn't it time you were on? Hurry up.

572
00:44:46,022 --> 00:44:48,274
Yes'm.

573
00:44:55,656 --> 00:44:57,617
Oooh... I like that expression.

574
00:44:57,700 --> 00:44:59,344
Try running your fingers through your hair.

575
00:44:59,368 --> 00:45:01,621
Oh, I like this.

576
00:45:01,704 --> 00:45:04,081
It's great!

577
00:45:05,917 --> 00:45:10,505
Perfume isn't for me.
And when I caught the scent...

578
00:45:10,588 --> 00:45:13,090
Yeah, just like that.
Part your lips a little...

579
00:45:13,174 --> 00:45:16,135
Great. Now let's take the top off too...

580
00:45:21,724 --> 00:45:25,478
I'd rather wear jeans...

581
00:45:25,520 --> 00:45:29,273
than tight business suits.

582
00:45:29,357 --> 00:45:35,530
This year, I'll not exert
myself and dress casually.

583
00:45:36,989 --> 00:45:44,956
I wanted to be a woman that suited you...

584
00:45:45,039 --> 00:45:48,876
but I knew we would
drift apart even if...

585
00:45:48,960 --> 00:45:55,216
I kept standing on my tippy-toes.

586
00:46:00,429 --> 00:46:02,306
I thought you decided
to go through with this!

587
00:46:02,390 --> 00:46:05,518
Everyone is waiting for you!

588
00:46:05,560 --> 00:46:07,979
Come on, Mima!

589
00:46:08,062 --> 00:46:11,190
See? Didn't I tell you?

590
00:46:12,233 --> 00:46:14,735
You were better off as a pop idol.

591
00:46:14,777 --> 00:46:17,154
Hey Mima, are you listening?

592
00:46:17,238 --> 00:46:20,324
Stop all this nonsense! Who are you!?

593
00:46:20,408 --> 00:46:23,494
Me? I'm a pop idol.

594
00:46:23,578 --> 00:46:25,621
Everyone's waiting for me.

595
00:46:25,705 --> 00:46:29,542
So I'm going to sing with
Rei and Yukiko again.

596
00:46:29,584 --> 00:46:31,085
No, I'm not!

597
00:46:31,127 --> 00:46:33,671
I'm an actress!

598
00:46:33,838 --> 00:46:35,089
Don't be silly!

599
00:46:35,131 --> 00:46:37,425
No one really wants that!

600
00:46:37,466 --> 00:46:39,051
Wait!

601
00:46:39,093 --> 00:46:40,678
What everyone wants is...

602
00:46:40,761 --> 00:46:44,724
from comics than difficult books and...

603
00:46:44,807 --> 00:46:49,395
I want to stay the way I am forever.

604
00:46:49,478 --> 00:46:52,607
Walking past, making a breeze...

605
00:46:52,690 --> 00:46:57,194
burning the scenery into my memories.

606
00:46:57,278 --> 00:47:00,281
I am fine even if I'm alone.

607
00:47:00,364 --> 00:47:08,364
I have finally found a
luxurious loneliness.

608
00:47:08,998 --> 00:47:11,000
Thank you, everyone!

609
00:47:23,638 --> 00:47:25,681
June 27th:
Thank you for coming to the event today!

610
00:47:25,765 --> 00:47:28,601
It really is the best feeling to
sing in front of all of you!

611
00:47:42,990 --> 00:47:44,742
BASTARDS!!

612
00:47:44,825 --> 00:47:48,287
Mima Kirigoe
Leaving the Throne of a Pop Idol!!

613
00:47:58,506 --> 00:47:59,382
Huh?

614
00:47:59,465 --> 00:48:01,592
Hey!

615
00:48:02,134 --> 00:48:04,303
What are you doing?

616
00:48:30,871 --> 00:48:32,599
To Mr. ME-MANIA:
Thank you for your e-mail every day...

617
00:48:32,623 --> 00:48:35,000
You believe me, right?

618
00:48:35,042 --> 00:48:37,795
That's not me. She's an impostor!

619
00:48:37,878 --> 00:48:40,297
Of course.
Mimarin would never do such a thing.

620
00:48:40,381 --> 00:48:42,842
I will protect you, the real Mimarin.

621
00:48:43,259 --> 00:48:47,680
I trust you, Mr. ME-MANIA.

622
00:48:47,722 --> 00:48:50,099
I won't change one bit.

623
00:48:50,182 --> 00:48:52,059
I'll always be with you.

624
00:48:52,143 --> 00:48:55,479
But that impostor keeps getting in my way.

625
00:48:55,563 --> 00:48:58,232
What should I do?

626
00:48:59,024 --> 00:49:02,987
I'll get rid of her.

627
00:49:03,821 --> 00:49:06,866
Thank you, Mr. Me-mania!

628
00:49:10,035 --> 00:49:12,997
You're the only one I can depend on.

629
00:49:23,215 --> 00:49:27,219
I don't know anything about myself anymore!

630
00:49:27,636 --> 00:49:28,596
Well...

631
00:49:28,637 --> 00:49:31,599
How do you think you know
that person you were...

632
00:49:31,640 --> 00:49:34,643
a second ago is the
same person you are now?

633
00:49:35,728 --> 00:49:37,813
A continuous stream of memories.

634
00:49:37,897 --> 00:49:41,317
Given only that, we all create
illusions within ourselves...

635
00:49:41,400 --> 00:49:44,862
saying that we each have
only one fixed persona.

636
00:49:44,945 --> 00:49:47,531
Doctor, I'm scared...

637
00:49:47,615 --> 00:49:51,202
that my other self will do something
that I don't know about...

638
00:49:52,161 --> 00:49:56,707
It's all right. There is no way
illusions can come to life.

639
00:50:01,837 --> 00:50:02,837
CUT!

640
00:50:04,423 --> 00:50:06,175
Mima, what's wrong?

641
00:50:06,258 --> 00:50:07,968
I'm sorry!

642
00:50:08,052 --> 00:50:10,846
Oh, man! This rain sucks!

643
00:50:10,930 --> 00:50:12,306
I think I'm going to catch a cold!

644
00:50:12,389 --> 00:50:14,683
I'm sorry!

645
00:50:22,483 --> 00:50:25,486
Wrap it up! Wrap it up!!

646
00:50:31,200 --> 00:50:36,705
It's pouring really badly outside, but
your heart is always, like, sunny!

647
00:50:36,789 --> 00:50:38,290
Well, I think we're ready today!

648
00:50:38,374 --> 00:50:38,958
Welcome to Rei...

649
00:50:38,999 --> 00:50:40,000
and Yukiko's...

650
00:50:40,042 --> 00:50:42,753
"Idol Chamland"!

651
00:50:45,506 --> 00:50:47,341
Mr. Tadokoro?

652
00:50:47,424 --> 00:50:49,176
I'm sure they're on the air now.

653
00:50:49,218 --> 00:50:51,378
I thought you'd like to see
them coz it's been a while.

654
00:50:54,390 --> 00:51:00,354
We have a show this Sunday.
It's at Ibaragi Sim City at 2pm.

655
00:51:00,437 --> 00:51:02,165
- How have you been?
- People from all over, come see us!

656
00:51:02,189 --> 00:51:05,568
- Just thought I'd drop by.
- We'll be waiting for you!

657
00:51:05,651 --> 00:51:09,738
Chamland will be back next week
at the same time. Until then...

658
00:51:09,822 --> 00:51:11,115
Two, three...

659
00:51:11,198 --> 00:51:12,658
Bye bye!

660
00:51:12,908 --> 00:51:15,661
Good show, guys.

661
00:51:16,203 --> 00:51:17,663
Hey, it's Mima.

662
00:51:20,749 --> 00:51:21,749
Mima!

663
00:51:51,238 --> 00:51:52,489
Wait!

664
00:51:54,241 --> 00:51:55,492
Who are you!?

665
00:52:04,001 --> 00:52:07,296
I told you! I'M the real Mima.

666
00:52:39,912 --> 00:52:42,706
In other news...

667
00:52:42,790 --> 00:52:46,168
Today, the Economic Planning Agency
announced a "New Citizen's Life Index"...

668
00:52:46,251 --> 00:52:49,713
that indicates the overall
Japanese standard of living and...

669
00:52:51,966 --> 00:52:54,760
It feels like I haven't
seen you in a long time.

670
00:52:54,802 --> 00:52:56,887
Well, I've been busy too.

671
00:52:56,971 --> 00:52:59,682
So, are you getting used to acting?

672
00:52:59,765 --> 00:53:01,100
Yeah.

673
00:53:01,183 --> 00:53:04,228
It's hard, but I chose to do it.

674
00:53:05,521 --> 00:53:07,648
You've matured quite a bit, Mima!

675
00:53:07,731 --> 00:53:11,235
But it's good that people
seem to like the new Mima.

676
00:53:12,611 --> 00:53:14,238
Yeah...

677
00:53:15,531 --> 00:53:18,075
That doesn't look like
a face that's agreeing.

678
00:53:18,158 --> 00:53:22,246
You know... Mima...
Has someone been harassing you?

679
00:53:23,831 --> 00:53:26,750
I've been visiting that home page.

680
00:53:27,167 --> 00:53:30,504
It's a bit much, even if it's a complaint
about how you changed your image...

681
00:53:31,422 --> 00:53:33,424
It's better if you didn't look at it.

682
00:53:33,507 --> 00:53:34,925
Yeah...

683
00:53:35,009 --> 00:53:37,428
But maybe she is more like me than myself.

684
00:53:37,511 --> 00:53:39,179
Mima?

685
00:53:39,221 --> 00:53:42,349
My other self that I buried
deep within my heart.

686
00:53:42,391 --> 00:53:43,434
What if...

687
00:53:43,517 --> 00:53:47,021
What if that other personality suddenly
started acting on its own?

688
00:53:47,104 --> 00:53:51,150
It's all right. There is no way
illusions can come to life.

689
00:53:51,233 --> 00:53:51,775
Rumi?

690
00:53:51,859 --> 00:53:52,693
CUT!

691
00:53:52,776 --> 00:53:55,904
Mima! What are you saying?

692
00:53:57,239 --> 00:54:00,868
I feel like I'm gonna have
nightmares about this line!

693
00:54:00,951 --> 00:54:03,162
I'm sorry!

694
00:54:13,255 --> 00:54:14,131
What's wrong?

695
00:54:14,214 --> 00:54:16,467
Uh, nothing...

696
00:54:20,804 --> 00:54:23,932
Once more, from the top...

697
00:54:25,768 --> 00:54:27,478
All right, Take 2!

698
00:54:30,647 --> 00:54:32,733
In other news...

699
00:54:32,816 --> 00:54:36,236
Today, the Economic Planning Agency
announced a "New Citizen's Life Index"...

700
00:54:36,278 --> 00:54:39,740
that indicates the overall
Japanese standard of living and...

701
00:54:41,784 --> 00:54:44,745
It's been a while, Rumi.

702
00:54:44,787 --> 00:54:48,248
What? I was here yesterday, too!

703
00:54:49,625 --> 00:54:53,212
Yesterday? Was that real?

704
00:54:54,630 --> 00:54:57,424
You're weird, Mima.

705
00:54:58,092 --> 00:55:00,260
Mima! What's wrong with you!?

706
00:55:00,302 --> 00:55:02,930
You're bleeding!

707
00:55:06,100 --> 00:55:08,936
This blood is real, isn't it?

708
00:55:09,019 --> 00:55:10,771
Mima!

709
00:55:14,566 --> 00:55:17,046
Today I went shopping in Harajuku.
I'm a sucker for sale items.

710
00:55:23,867 --> 00:55:27,037
I guess... I went to Harajuku today...

711
00:55:34,837 --> 00:55:36,213
You mean...

712
00:55:36,296 --> 00:55:39,633
the murderer is an illusion she created?

713
00:55:39,716 --> 00:55:40,716
Yes.

714
00:55:41,510 --> 00:55:43,846
She fears an imaginary security guard...

715
00:55:43,929 --> 00:55:48,600
and then doubles that figure with
the serial murderer of top models.

716
00:55:49,143 --> 00:55:51,645
But illusions don't kill.

717
00:55:52,771 --> 00:55:56,942
But... what if that illusion found
someone to possess?

718
00:55:57,025 --> 00:55:58,485
Possess??

719
00:55:58,569 --> 00:56:00,863
Then... all those men who got murdered?

720
00:56:00,946 --> 00:56:04,658
Were those who were no
longer of any use to her.

721
00:56:05,826 --> 00:56:08,412
Find her quickly, Mr. Yamashiro.

722
00:56:08,495 --> 00:56:12,124
Before another victim falls prey.

723
00:56:15,627 --> 00:56:18,005
How much?

724
00:56:22,551 --> 00:56:25,179
You sure are a weird pizza man.

725
00:57:00,714 --> 00:57:03,467
Stop! Please stop!

726
00:57:15,270 --> 00:57:19,399
Yeah, that looks good... Come on,
be more daring! More passionate!

727
00:57:32,496 --> 00:57:33,872
All right! Take three!

728
00:57:51,932 --> 00:57:52,766
- Hello?
- Mima?

729
00:57:52,808 --> 00:57:55,310
Are you all right over there?

730
00:57:55,352 --> 00:57:57,604
You haven't heard yet... about Mr. Murano?

731
00:58:00,482 --> 00:58:01,608
Can't be!

732
00:58:02,693 --> 00:58:05,904
Police say that Murano died
of multiple stab wounds...

733
00:58:05,988 --> 00:58:07,823
Mr. Murano!? Really!?

734
00:58:07,864 --> 00:58:11,118
We're going crazy here!

735
00:58:11,702 --> 00:58:14,955
Anyway, stay put until
I get there. All right!?

736
00:58:14,997 --> 00:58:18,458
The weapon used in the latest murder
is said to closely resemble...

737
00:58:18,542 --> 00:58:22,170
the one used in last week's killing
of a popular screenwriter.

738
00:58:22,254 --> 00:58:26,049
Police are considering a personal
grudge as the motive...

739
00:58:26,133 --> 00:58:30,137
and are looking into connections
between the two cases.

740
00:59:00,584 --> 00:59:04,838
Miss Kirigoe! Please, can we get your
opinion about the murder of Mr. Murano?

741
00:59:04,880 --> 00:59:06,548
Do you know anything?

742
00:59:06,631 --> 00:59:10,427
Isn't there a connection with the killing
of Mr. Shibuya the screenwriter?

743
00:59:10,510 --> 00:59:13,430
Miss Kirigoe!
There are rumors of a love triangle...

744
00:59:13,513 --> 00:59:16,516
between you, Mr. Shibuya,
and Mr. Murano and we...

745
00:59:21,855 --> 00:59:23,982
You think she's jinxed?

746
00:59:24,066 --> 00:59:26,234
What happens twice happens thrice.

747
00:59:26,318 --> 00:59:28,111
Let's take bets on who's next.

748
00:59:28,195 --> 00:59:29,654
Cut it out!

749
00:59:29,738 --> 00:59:32,574
Don't mind them.

750
00:59:32,657 --> 00:59:35,535
Am I alive?

751
00:59:35,577 --> 00:59:42,042
Maybe that truck hit me...
and this is all a dream...

752
00:59:42,125 --> 00:59:44,461
Everyone ready?

753
00:59:44,544 --> 00:59:46,922
OK. Mima!

754
00:59:52,969 --> 00:59:55,847
Breathe harder than during rehearsal.

755
00:59:55,931 --> 00:59:58,100
You've just killed someone.

756
00:59:58,183 --> 00:59:59,935
Yes.

757
01:00:11,279 --> 01:00:13,865
And... action!

758
01:00:22,582 --> 01:00:25,127
Are you awake?

759
01:00:27,963 --> 01:00:29,131
You are?

760
01:00:29,214 --> 01:00:31,716
Can you tell me your name?

761
01:00:32,300 --> 01:00:35,595
Me? I'm Mima Kirigoe.

762
01:00:35,637 --> 01:00:37,556
Okay. And what do you do?

763
01:00:37,639 --> 01:00:41,726
I'm a pop idol... no, an actress.

764
01:00:42,352 --> 01:00:44,521
That must be hard work.

765
01:00:44,604 --> 01:00:48,191
It's hard, but it's what I chose to do.

766
01:00:49,151 --> 01:00:53,530
She thinks she's a new young
actress named Mima Kirigoe.

767
01:00:57,993 --> 01:01:01,121
Dissociative Identity Disorder.

768
01:01:01,913 --> 01:01:04,082
In other words,
"multiple personality syndrome."

769
01:01:04,166 --> 01:01:09,087
All those crimes took place when
she was some other persona.

770
01:01:09,171 --> 01:01:12,424
So where's the persona
of the original Yoko?

771
01:01:12,507 --> 01:01:15,051
Yoko Takakura, the original persona...

772
01:01:15,135 --> 01:01:19,431
is nothing more than a character
in a drama for her.

773
01:01:20,182 --> 01:01:24,686
Being a "normal" girl... how she
was raped in a strip club...

774
01:01:24,769 --> 01:01:27,272
Everything happened as
part of her drama series.

775
01:01:27,355 --> 01:01:30,901
By doing so, she salvaged her heart.

776
01:01:33,820 --> 01:01:37,073
That's right. I'm an actress.

777
01:01:37,657 --> 01:01:39,784
Cut!

778
01:01:42,120 --> 01:01:44,247
Can you tell me your name?

779
01:01:44,331 --> 01:01:47,667
Me? I'm Rika Takakura.

780
01:01:48,293 --> 01:01:52,088
The original persona,
Yoko Takakura, no longer exists.

781
01:01:52,172 --> 01:01:58,261
By killing, and later becoming, her sister
the top-model, she salvaged her heart.

782
01:02:01,306 --> 01:02:04,601
That's right. I'm a model.

783
01:02:04,684 --> 01:02:07,854
All right! That's the take!

784
01:02:17,531 --> 01:02:19,324
We did it, Mima!

785
01:02:19,407 --> 01:02:22,869
Mima... Good work!

786
01:02:22,953 --> 01:02:24,788
I can tell you tried so hard!

787
01:02:24,871 --> 01:02:26,206
Rumi...

788
01:02:26,248 --> 01:02:30,752
As of this moment,
Double Bind is in the can!

789
01:02:30,835 --> 01:02:33,213
Everyone, great job!

790
01:02:51,273 --> 01:02:54,234
You were fantastic, Mima!
What do you think, Director?

791
01:02:54,317 --> 01:02:56,528
She really was excellent.

792
01:02:56,611 --> 01:02:58,238
Thanks a lot.

793
01:02:58,280 --> 01:02:59,864
See you at the wrap-up party.

794
01:02:59,948 --> 01:03:03,076
We'll be talking to you.

795
01:03:03,118 --> 01:03:04,911
Then... shall we go as well?

796
01:03:04,953 --> 01:03:07,372
Mima, go get changed.

797
01:03:22,804 --> 01:03:23,555
Dr. Touko...

798
01:03:23,638 --> 01:03:27,851
Hey now! I'm not Touko anymore!
Did you forget?

799
01:03:27,934 --> 01:03:32,314
"There is no way illusions
can come to life."

800
01:03:32,397 --> 01:03:34,858
You should stop dreaming soon.

801
01:03:46,453 --> 01:03:47,954
Eri?

802
01:03:51,333 --> 01:03:53,585
What's taking Mima so long?

803
01:03:53,668 --> 01:03:57,797
I'm going back to the office.
Take Mima home, will ya?

804
01:03:57,881 --> 01:04:01,468
Mr. Tadokoro. You were saying something
about Mima's next job?

805
01:04:02,427 --> 01:04:04,471
Oh, it's great!

806
01:04:04,512 --> 01:04:06,139
A starring role in a video movie.

807
01:04:06,222 --> 01:04:10,602
There are a few sketchy scenes...
but what can you do?

808
01:04:14,564 --> 01:04:16,775
Somebody help me!

809
01:04:18,443 --> 01:04:22,113
Like anyone can hear
YOUR voice right now!

810
01:04:24,449 --> 01:04:25,492
Who are you!?

811
01:04:25,575 --> 01:04:26,868
Why are you doing this!?

812
01:04:26,951 --> 01:04:29,704
I'm protecting my dear Mimarin!

813
01:04:29,788 --> 01:04:32,123
But-But I'm Mima!

814
01:04:34,042 --> 01:04:36,002
No, no, no, no, NO!

815
01:04:36,086 --> 01:04:38,838
You didn't know I was Me-mania!

816
01:04:38,880 --> 01:04:42,300
You're just PRETENDING to be Mimarin!

817
01:04:42,384 --> 01:04:43,426
STOP!

818
01:04:43,510 --> 01:04:45,887
NO! STOP!

819
01:04:50,517 --> 01:04:54,020
Did you fool that screenwriter and that
photographer with this little mouth?

820
01:04:54,062 --> 01:04:56,648
You tarnished Mimarin's name!

821
01:04:58,149 --> 01:05:00,819
Can it be... that you...

822
01:05:00,902 --> 01:05:04,531
The real Mimarin e-mails me every day!

823
01:05:04,614 --> 01:05:06,574
And she says that you
keep getting in her way!

824
01:05:06,616 --> 01:05:08,493
You killed them!?

825
01:05:08,576 --> 01:05:10,704
And you'll die soon, too!

826
01:05:24,759 --> 01:05:26,052
Bad girl!

827
01:05:26,136 --> 01:05:29,431
You have to follow the script!

828
01:05:33,101 --> 01:05:34,436
And now... TAKE 2!

829
01:07:10,532 --> 01:07:12,492
All right! Looks good!!

830
01:07:16,037 --> 01:07:18,540
You're the best, Mima!

831
01:07:35,682 --> 01:07:37,725
Mima!

832
01:07:38,560 --> 01:07:40,687
What's wrong? You're in shambles!

833
01:07:40,770 --> 01:07:43,606
I was looking all over for you!

834
01:07:43,690 --> 01:07:44,482
Rumi...

835
01:07:44,566 --> 01:07:47,026
What in the world happened?

836
01:07:58,162 --> 01:08:00,123
This can't be!!

837
01:08:00,206 --> 01:08:04,043
Are you sure you weren't dreaming?

838
01:08:14,929 --> 01:08:17,140
Are you all right?

839
01:08:17,223 --> 01:08:20,894
I'm taking you back... to Mima's room.

840
01:08:41,497 --> 01:08:43,666
Rumi, are you here?

841
01:08:43,750 --> 01:08:45,084
What?

842
01:08:45,168 --> 01:08:47,712
Oh, nothing...

843
01:08:49,255 --> 01:08:51,716
Oh, that's right,
I have to call Mr. Tadokoro.

844
01:09:51,859 --> 01:09:56,197
No... This isn't my room...

845
01:09:56,239 --> 01:09:59,784
Of course not! This is Mima's room!

846
01:10:01,160 --> 01:10:02,537
You're!

847
01:10:02,578 --> 01:10:05,873
Look! It's the new costume!

848
01:10:06,958 --> 01:10:09,002
I'm wearing it at tomorrow's show!

849
01:10:09,085 --> 01:10:12,505
Isn't it great? It's perfect on me!

850
01:10:14,966 --> 01:10:16,884
Rumi? Why?

851
01:10:18,886 --> 01:10:20,680
Rumi?

852
01:10:20,722 --> 01:10:23,349
Rumi...

853
01:10:23,391 --> 01:10:25,727
Oh! Rumi went home.

854
01:10:25,768 --> 01:10:28,146
She said she's been busy lately
and was deprived of sleep.

855
01:10:28,229 --> 01:10:30,690
Don't say weird stuff like that!

856
01:10:30,773 --> 01:10:32,316
This is a joke, isn't it, Rumi!?

857
01:10:32,400 --> 01:10:35,695
Love makes your heart race.

858
01:10:35,737 --> 01:10:39,699
If it means you're loved in the end...

859
01:10:39,741 --> 01:10:41,743
What do you think? Perfect, huh?

860
01:10:41,784 --> 01:10:44,662
A pop idol HAS to sing, after all!

861
01:10:44,746 --> 01:10:46,122
But...

862
01:10:46,205 --> 01:10:48,332
You just had to keep getting in my way.

863
01:10:48,416 --> 01:10:50,668
Rumi was totally furious, too.

864
01:10:50,752 --> 01:10:53,546
Please... stop all of this!

865
01:10:53,588 --> 01:10:57,842
But a pop idol is always
protected by her fans!

866
01:10:57,925 --> 01:11:01,095
They listen to any favor
I, Mima, ask them!

867
01:11:01,179 --> 01:11:04,766
Although Mr. Me-mania failed a wee bit...

868
01:11:04,849 --> 01:11:08,603
Me-mania?
How do you know him!?

869
01:11:09,228 --> 01:11:14,108
But, oh, well..." you reap what you
sow," especially about YOU.

870
01:12:56,127 --> 01:12:58,880
Help! Somebody help me!

871
01:13:11,559 --> 01:13:13,728
Please! Rumi, it's you, isn't it!?

872
01:13:13,811 --> 01:13:15,229
PLEASE WAKE UP!

873
01:13:15,313 --> 01:13:18,232
YOU'RE the one who needs to wake up!

874
01:13:24,697 --> 01:13:27,575
Help, help, somebody!

875
01:13:28,075 --> 01:13:31,037
Help! SOMEBODY HELP ME!

876
01:13:35,249 --> 01:13:38,544
SOMEBODY! SOMEBODY HELP ME!!

877
01:13:42,089 --> 01:13:45,218
HELP! SOMEBODY HELP ME!

878
01:14:14,789 --> 01:14:16,791
Let's end all of this.

879
01:14:16,874 --> 01:14:19,126
We don't need two Mimas!

880
01:14:19,210 --> 01:14:20,878
I AM MIMA!

881
01:14:21,963 --> 01:14:25,049
That's funny! Mima is a pop idol!

882
01:14:25,132 --> 01:14:27,468
You're just a dirty old impostor!

883
01:14:27,551 --> 01:14:31,430
LIKE I CARE! I AM WHO I AM!!

884
01:15:40,708 --> 01:15:41,584
Oh, shit!

885
01:15:41,667 --> 01:15:44,003
Get the police!
No, call an ambulance!

886
01:15:44,086 --> 01:15:46,339
I know!

887
01:16:44,730 --> 01:16:48,317
Thank you for the flowers you always bring.

888
01:16:48,401 --> 01:16:50,194
I'll put them in my room.

889
01:16:50,236 --> 01:16:53,823
They're pretty. Very pretty...

890
01:17:00,246 --> 01:17:04,583
I didn't know you were visiting.
You must be very busy lately.

891
01:17:04,625 --> 01:17:05,751
Oh, no.

892
01:17:05,835 --> 01:17:09,797
Once in a while, she returns
to her Rumi persona, but...

893
01:17:09,880 --> 01:17:13,259
I know I'll never see HER ever again.

894
01:17:13,676 --> 01:17:18,764
But, thanks to her,
I am who I am today.

895
01:17:28,482 --> 01:17:31,944
You're lying! There's no way Mima
Kirigoe would be HERE of all places!

896
01:17:31,986 --> 01:17:33,946
I guess she was just a look-alike.

897
01:17:43,164 --> 01:17:45,583
No, I'm real!

898
01:18:02,808 --> 01:18:08,856
Each time I pass this
station on the train...

899
01:18:08,939 --> 01:18:16,322
my heart fills with nostalgia.

900
01:18:16,405 --> 01:18:24,405
The days when I ran around town,
hiding all of my feelings...

901
01:18:26,874 --> 01:18:31,003
in my school uniform.

902
01:18:31,045 --> 01:18:37,718
Take me to the first time I was in love...

903
01:18:37,801 --> 01:18:45,801
those four seasons when
I was frantic yet doubtful.

904
01:18:45,893 --> 01:18:52,566
Remember all those times when
just being near each other...

905
01:18:52,650 --> 01:19:00,650
kept our love for each other growing?

906
01:19:17,341 --> 01:19:23,264
I cut my hair after graduation.

907
01:19:23,347 --> 01:19:30,854
I wonder if you are still the same.

908
01:19:30,896 --> 01:19:38,896
Are you still pursuing that dream
that you kept telling me about...

909
01:19:41,282 --> 01:19:45,369
on the way home?

910
01:19:45,452 --> 01:19:52,251
Take me to when my tears overflowed...

911
01:19:52,293 --> 01:20:00,293
to those four seasons that
I felt from the bottom of my heart.

912
01:20:00,384 --> 01:20:07,057
Remember how in the sunsets after school...

913
01:20:07,141 --> 01:20:15,141
we just wanted time to spend alone?

914
01:20:30,247 --> 01:20:36,837
Even in this new season, I can't shake...

915
01:20:36,920 --> 01:20:44,920
the habit of bluffing when I am sad.

916
01:20:45,095 --> 01:20:51,727
I'm sure that you knew.

917
01:20:51,810 --> 01:20:59,810
I still remember your eyes when
you looked at me silently.
